{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"d1","type":"claim","text":"The written-agreement trial's defensible role, after the objection's b4 and the rival's m2, is diagnostic rather than remedial: a short, cheap instrument with a pre-registered verdict question. Run as the fix, it inherits the disease it treats; run as a test, it sorts recall failure from standards or interest conflict.","grounds":"b4 shows the trial needs a pre-agreed success criterion; b5 and o1 show its promised consequence is overstated; m2 supplies the diagnostic framing.","scope":"Household chore coordination","revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a4"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#b4","h005.fork5.p.response.1#b5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#m2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#o1"]},{"id":"d2","type":"commitment","text":"Propose to the household a two-week trial of one-line shared records (named person, done-criterion, time), framed openly as a test rather than a new regime, with the verdict question recorded alongside the first entry: after two weeks, are we still arguing, and about what?","action":"Run a two-week minimal written-record trial with a pre-registered verdict question","consequence":"Each outcome -- disputes vanish, disputes mutate into interpretation or standards, records refused, gamed, or never produced -- is itself informative and has a pre-named next step; non-production is branch evidence, so the avoiding friend's silence cannot silently void the test.","scope":"Next two weeks","depends":["d1"]},{"id":"d3","type":"claim","text":"Under the diagnostic framing, resistance to or gaming of the record is evidence rather than defeat: litigating criteria, neglecting to record, or retro-narrowing agreements are observable patterns indicating interest or standards conflict. Neither innocence nor motivated vagueness has to be assumed in advance.","bearing":"Answers most of b1's force; does not resolve b6's residual gamer -- the plan routes around such a person but remediates nothing, and if routing fails the question moves to the viability of the arrangement.","depends":["d2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#b1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#b6"]},{"id":"d4","type":"commitment","text":"Attach three pre-named branches to the trial verdict. (i) Disputes vanish: build the account's fuller written system, weekly reset included. (ii) Disputes mutate into what-counts, exceptions, or standards fights: move to domain ownership or rotating full weeks with turn-picking or credit-bidding for the unequal split, or buy cleaning if budget allows; an exposed imbalance of effort is handled here by renegotiating the split itself, absorbing a7. (iii) Trial refused, gamed, or yielding no recordable agreements: one structured one-time ownership conversation, then unilateral scope declaration, then the viability question.","action":"Pre-register a three-branch response table alongside the trial","consequence":"Coordination costs (a fuller written system) and relocation costs (a one-time ownership negotiation, itself nontrivial per q2) are incurred only when the trial indicates they address the actual driver.","depends":["d2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#c2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#c3","h005.fork5.p.response.1#b7","h005.fork5.p.response.2#q2"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a7"]},{"id":"d5","type":"commitment","text":"Keep the asynchronous channel for the avoiding friend as a low-cost input route to the conversation, but drop the 'full participation' clause: participation in talk is not contribution to household labor, and contribution is judged by observable outcomes -- which owned domains make directly visible without requiring the friend's attendance at anything.","action":"Offer the channel as input route; judge contribution by outcomes, not edits","revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a5"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#b2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#o2"]},{"id":"d6","type":"claim","text":"Sequencing answers the proportionality objection without conceding the institutional diagnosis as a premise: the minimal record is nearly costless, so bureaucratization costs are paid only if the test says coordination infrastructure will work, and decoupling's own negotiation cost (q2) is paid only when evidence points there. Recall failure and institution failure remain live hypotheses until the test runs.","bearing":"Preserves most of b3's and c1's force while declining to replace the coordination strategy family outright.","depends":["d2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#b3","h005.fork5.p.response.2#c1"]},{"id":"d7","type":"objection","text":"The unilateral scope declaration converts a coordination failure into a contest of tolerances and spends friendship capital by design -- the visible lapse is leverage. It is rational only after a structured attempt has failed, only if the asker can genuinely tolerate undone chores longer than the others can, and in acknowledged tension with a6's separation of friendship from chore-negotiation.","target":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#m1"],"bearing":"Demotes the move to the late branch of d4 rather than rejecting it."},{"id":"d8","type":"use","text":"Retain unchanged: the calm scheduled meta-conversation raising the pattern rather than the latest incident, with friendship talk kept separate (a6), and the flag that refusal across all channels changes the question from chore management to the viability of the living arrangement (a8, also retained by u1). The weekly reset, which the objection noted had no commitments record, moves into branch (i) of d4 as part of the fuller system the test may endorse.","target":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#a6","h005.fork5.p.response.0#a8"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#u1"]},{"id":"d9","type":"problem","text":"Left open: which driver obtains (deliberately -- the trial exists to answer it); whether the one-time ownership negotiation succeeds where repeated informal ones failed (q2); the size of the standards gap, available budget, and remaining goodwill; and the residual case of a flatmate who attends everything and games everything (b6), where the branch structure defers rather than solves the interest conflict.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#q1","h005.fork5.p.response.2#q2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#b6"]}],"uptake":["d1","d2","d3","d4","d5","d6","d7","d8","d9"]}